From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btusb: Request the reset GPIO only where a handler uses it

When onboard_usb_dev powers a WiFi/Bluetooth combo chip, the enable line
of the chip is the reset-gpios property of its USB device node, and
onboard_usb_dev holds that line. btusb asks for a "reset" GPIO on the same
node for every device and ends the probe on any error, so it fails with
-EBUSY and the Bluetooth function of the chip stays unbound. Seen on the
Radxa Cubie A7S with an AIC8800D80: no hci0.

Only the reset handlers of Intel, QCA and Realtek devices use this line
(btusb_intel_reset(), btusb_qca_reset(), btusb_rtl_reset()). Request it for
those devices only. For them nothing changes, a failure to get the line
still ends the probe. All other devices, MediaTek included whose reset
handler is btmtk_reset_sync(), never used the line after the request at
probe. On a combo chip a btusb reset through it would also cut the WiFi
function.

A combo chip of one of these vendors behind onboard_usb_dev still
collides; that needs the reset to go through onboard_usb_dev.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -4162,13 +4162,20 @@ static int btusb_probe(struct usb_interface *intf,
 
 	SET_HCIDEV_DEV(hdev, &intf->dev);
 
-	reset_gpio = gpiod_get_optional(&data->udev->dev, "reset",
-					GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
-	if (IS_ERR(reset_gpio)) {
-		err = PTR_ERR(reset_gpio);
-		goto out_free_dev;
-	} else if (reset_gpio) {
-		data->reset_gpio = reset_gpio;
+	/* Only the Intel, QCA and Realtek reset handlers use the reset line.
+	 * On other devices it may belong to another driver, such as
+	 * onboard_usb_dev powering a WiFi/Bluetooth combo chip.
+	 */
+	if (id->driver_info & (BTUSB_INTEL_COMBINED | BTUSB_QCA_ROME |
+			       BTUSB_QCA_WCN6855 | BTUSB_REALTEK)) {
+		reset_gpio = gpiod_get_optional(&data->udev->dev, "reset",
+						GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+		if (IS_ERR(reset_gpio)) {
+			err = PTR_ERR(reset_gpio);
+			goto out_free_dev;
+		} else if (reset_gpio) {
+			data->reset_gpio = reset_gpio;
+		}
 	}
 
 	hdev->open    = btusb_open;
